  "processNotes": {
    "state": "present",
    "source": "retro.json",
    "author": "implementer",
    "independent": false,
    "summary": "Second repair round. The IT service desk feature that the previous round left unwired is now complete and verified end to end against a running application: migration, role-scoped server service, authenticated /api routes, screenshot upload/download, in-app notifications with ticket route targets, the 24h service-desk reminder, six client pages behind declared routes and navigation, both locales, and logic tests. Four runtime defects were found and fixed during this round: sample data never registered (provider register/boot ordering), the ticket router doubled its prefix, a datetime field was filtered with the string builder, and a wildcard auth middleware leaked from the merged router into every later /api contribution. Full UI workflow browser acceptance was not performed; see the open blocker.",
    "blockers": [
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/B1",
        "phase": "implementation",
        "title": "Ticket write-field lists fail ESLint with a redundant type intersection",
        "symptom": "server/itsm/resources.ts lines 58, 66, 77 and 91 reported @typescript-eslint/no-redundant-type-constituents: `string` is overridden by the ServiceTicketRow key union in the intersection type `keyof ServiceTicketRow & string`.",
        "rootCause": "ServiceTicketRow declares only string-named fields, so `keyof ServiceTicketRow` is already a subset of string. Intersecting it with `string` collapses and the rule reports the redundant `string` constituent.",
        "resolution": "Changed the four `satisfies readonly (keyof ServiceTicketRow & string)[]` clauses to `satisfies readonly (keyof ServiceTicketRow)[]`, which still validates every listed write field against the row interface. Repo-wide `eslint . --max-warnings 0` passes.",
        "cost": null,
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/B2",
        "phase": "implementation",
        "title": "server/itsm declarations did not type-check",
        "symptom": "tsconfig.server.json reported TS2322 at server/itsm/record-access.ts:74 (rows.map((row) => row.id) returned unknown[] instead of number[]) and TS2314 at server/itsm/resources.ts:237 (CompositeResourceReference requires one type argument).",
        "rootCause": "The Kysely query result row is untyped, so `id` is `unknown`; and the authorization package now makes CompositeResourceReference generic over CompositeResourceActions.",
        "resolution": "Typed the selected id in the map callback (`row.id as number`) and declared the return type as `CompositeResourceReference<CompositeResourceActions>` with the type imported from @nocobase/authorization/core. `pnpm exec tsc -p tsconfig.server.json --noEmit` passes.",
        "cost": null,
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/B3",
        "phase": "implementation",
        "title": "IT service desk feature was not wired or complete",
        "symptom": "The working tree contained only database/main/migrations/202611150001_create_service_tickets.ts and server/itsm/{resources,record-access}.ts. Nothing called registerItsmResources or registerItsmRecordAccess; there were no server routes, no 24h reminder, no notification integration, no client routes/pages/dashboard, no locales, no seeds and no tests. The QA stage confirmed the delivered client bundle had no business keywords and /main/tickets redirected to /main.",
        "rootCause": "The implementation agent stopped after a context overflow at the schema/authorization-declaration stage, so the feature was never composed into the application.",
        "resolution": "Built and wired the whole module: server/itsm/{service,permission-sets,record-access,resources,sample-data}.ts, server/providers/itsm.ts (registered in server/providers/index.ts), server/routes/{schemas,tickets,files,index}.ts, the inbox notification channel, database/main/migrations/202611150001_create_service_tickets.ts, client/hooks/itsm.ts, client/components/itsm/status-badge.tsx, client/pages/{dashboard,tickets,team}, client/routes.ts with a service-desk navigation group, both locales, and tests. The redundant default landing page (client/pages/home) was removed so the dashboard owns `/`. The built client bundle now contains `service-desk`, `ticket/:ticketId`, and the tickets/team/dashboard route ids and locale keys.",
        "cost": null,
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/B4",
        "phase": "repair",
        "title": "Sample data silently never registered",
        "symptom": "Signing in as the sample users employee/dispatcher/engineer returned 401 INVALID_USERNAME_OR_PASSWORD even with APP_SAMPLE_DATA=true, so no demo tickets or role users existed.",
        "rootCause": "registerItsmSampleData ran in ItsmProvider.register() and used app.container.resolveIfCreated(sampleDataToken). The sample-data service is registered by the database provider, whose register() can run after an application provider's, so the token did not exist yet and the call returned undefined without recording anything.",
        "resolution": "Moved registerItsmSampleData into ItsmProvider.boot(). All providers have registered by boot and the application runs the registered samples after every provider is ready, so the sample is both registered in time and still executes with the full container. Verified with `pnpm nocobase db sample` (lists itsm/service-desk) and by signing in as all three role users and reading their scoped ticket lists.",
        "cost": null,
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/B5",
        "phase": "repair",
        "title": "Ticket API routes answered under a doubled prefix",
        "symptom": "The documented GET /api/tickets returned 404 while GET /api/tickets/tickets answered the list; Swagger showed /api/tickets/tickets.",
        "rootCause": "The contribution's createRouter mounted an inner router that already declared `/tickets` at `router.route('/tickets', routes)`. defineApiRoutes contributions are themselves mounted at `/api`, so the segment appeared twice.",
        "resolution": "Changed the mount to `router.route('/', routes)` and added tests/logic/itsm-route-mount.test.ts, which requests `/tickets` on the contributed router and asserts 200 with the list payload.",
        "cost": null,
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/B6",
        "phase": "repair",
        "title": "Datetime field filtered with the string builder",
        "symptom": "GET /api/tickets/dashboard and GET /api/tickets/engineers returned 400 with RepositoryError: Filter group \"string\" does not match Field \"disabledAt\" of type \"datetime\".",
        "rootCause": "listEngineers() used f.string('disabledAt').empty() on the datetime column that records a deactivated user.",
        "resolution": "Changed both occurrences to f.date('disabledAt').empty(). Verified the dashboard and engineers endpoints return 200 at runtime.",
        "cost": null,
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/B7",
        "phase": "repair",
        "title": "Wildcard auth middleware leaked into unrelated API contributions",
        "symptom": "tests/logic/app-server.test.ts failed: GET /api/articles, /api/example and /api/routesExample returned 401 instead of the expected JSON 404 ROUTE_NOT_FOUND.",
        "rootCause": "The ticket router registered `routes.use('*', auth.required())` and then mounted that inner router at the contribution root. The application merges every API contribution into one `/api` router, and Hono copies a mounted sub-router's middleware into the parent, so the wildcard authenticated every contribution mounted after the tickets.",
        "resolution": "Scoped the guard to the paths the contribution owns — `routes.use('/tickets', required)` and `routes.use('/tickets/*', required)`. Added a test that merges the ticket router into a parent and asserts a sibling path stays reachable, so the leak cannot return silently. Verified at runtime: anonymous /api/tickets is 401 while anonymous /api/articles is 404.",
        "cost": null,
        "status": "resolved"
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/B8",
        "phase": "verification",
        "title": "Full UI workflow browser acceptance was not performed",
        "symptom": "The full UI workflow calls for a design review and one independent browser acceptance review of the running interface; this repair ran under a reduced budget and no browser was installed for the application under test.",
        "rootCause": "Playwright browsers were not available in the environment and installing them exceeded the repair budget.",
        "resolution": "Not performed. Server behaviour was verified end to end with real HTTP requests (role-scoped lists, the full assign → process → resolve → confirm workflow, the return path, notifications with /tickets/{id} targets, the 24h reminder, screenshot upload/download and anonymous rejection), and the client route tree, locale coverage and pages are covered by logic tests and by the built bundle containing the routes and copy. A browser pass over the rendered pages, the clickable notification target and the overlay navigation remains for a full-budget verification round.",
        "cost": null,
        "status": "open"
      }
    ],
    "improvements": [
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/I1",
        "category": "pipeline",
        "title": "Surface lint and type failures in the same verification round",
        "detail": "The verification run stopped at lint and hid two real TypeScript errors in the same new files. A repair agent that only reads the reported lint failure leaves the next round to rediscover them.",
        "suggestedChange": "Run the type check alongside or before lint and aggregate both results into one failure report, or let lint continue so all static checks report in a single round.",
        "mechanizable": true
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/I2",
        "category": "framework",
        "title": "A route contribution should not be able to authenticate another contribution",
        "detail": "Registering `router.use('*', auth.required())` inside an API contribution silently widened the guard to every contribution mounted after it, because the application merges all API contributions into one router and Hono copies mounted middleware into the parent. The failure appeared in an unrelated template test, far from the code that caused it.",
        "suggestedChange": "Have app-server reject or warn at start when an API contribution registers middleware whose resolved path is `*` (or otherwise escapes the paths the contribution also defines), and document that guards belong on the exact owned paths.",
        "mechanizable": true
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/38969434205/attempt/1/I3",
        "category": "verification",
        "title": "A sample-data check must start from a fresh install",
        "detail": "Sample data only runs when the default connection is installed with app.sampleData set, then is recorded as skipped on every later start. A verification that reuses an existing development database therefore reports no sample data without the sample code being at fault, which is exactly how this round's missing users first appeared.",
        "suggestedChange": "When a task declares sample data, have the runtime verification install against a fresh database (or run `nocobase db sample`) before asserting the sample users and records exist.",
        "mechanizable": true
      }
    ],
    "note": "实现者自述，未经独立核验；不是框架评审结论。"
